course: dictionary
lesson: 1522
title: Central: middle, main, or one main place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Central has more than one meaning, so context decides which one you need. «The central square was full of people on market day.» Central means in the middle here, because the square is the middle of the town. Try the swap: "the middle square" makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The central idea of the story is that kindness matters.» Here central means most important or main. Swap in "the main idea" and it still works. Words that sit next to central, like square, idea or heating, give you the clue.
explain: Central also appears in names of places, like «Central America» and «Central Asia». These are names of large regions, so you learn them as a phrase. «Central heating» is another phrase: one boiler sends warmth to the whole house, so central means controlled from one main place.
fact: Central means in the middle or centre of something.
fact: Central can mean most important or main, as in «the central idea of a story».
fact: Central can mean controlled from one main place, as in «central heating».
fact: Names of regions use central with a capital letter, such as «Central America» and «Central Asia».
fact: In the UK, the middle of a city is called the «city centre»; in the US it is often called «downtown».
exercise: «The central square was full of people on market day.» What does central mean here? | Very dangerous | *In the middle of the town | Quiet and empty | Very old
exercise: «The central idea of the story is that kindness matters.» What is central in this sentence? | The shortest | Silly | *The most important | The last part of the book
exercise: «Macaws live in the forests of Central and South America.» What does Central mean here? | Warm, like a heater | *Part of the name of a region, Central America | The middle of a forest | Controlled from one main place
test: «Central heating» warms a whole house from one boiler. What does central mean in this phrase? | Most important | In the middle of a square | *Controlled from one main place | Very warm and sunny
test: Which sentence uses central to mean most important? | Stand in the central part of the hall | The central heating was broken | Central America has many forests | *The central character is a brave girl who saves her village
exam: «The Black Death probably started in Central Asia.» Why is Central used here? | It means in the middle of a room | *It is part of the region name Central Asia | It means most important | It means controlled from one place
